@startuml Email Pipeline End-to-End Flow

title Email Intelligence Pipeline - Complete Flow

actor User as U
participant "Web Browser" as WB
participant "Flask App" as FA
participant "Chat Controller" as CC
participant "Email Management Controller" as EMC
participant "Email Indexer" as EI
participant "Gmail OAuth Service" as GOS
participant "Gmail API" as GAPI
participant "Email Fetcher" as EF
participant "Gmail Langchain Service" as GLS
participant "Email Vector Store" as EVS
participant "Chroma DB" as CDB
participant "Email RAG Handler" as ERH
participant "LLM (Grok/OpenAI/Gemini)" as LLM
participant "Sentence Transformer" as ST

== Email Setup & Authentication ==
U -> WB: Access Email Intelligence
WB -> FA: GET /email/config-status
FA -> EMC: get_config_status()
EMC -> GOS: Check OAuth configuration
GOS --> EMC: OAuth status
EMC --> FA: Configuration status
FA --> WB: Show setup requirements

U -> WB: Connect Gmail Account
WB -> FA: GET /email/oauth
FA -> GOS: Initiate OAuth flow
GOS -> GAPI: OAuth authorization
GAPI --> GOS: Authorization code
GOS --> FA: OAuth success
FA --> WB: Gmail connected

== Email Indexing Pipeline ==
U -> WB: Index Emails
WB -> FA: POST /email/index
FA -> EMC: index_emails()
EMC -> EI: index_user_emails()

EI -> GOS: get_gmail_service(user_id)
GOS -> GAPI: Get Gmail service
GAPI --> GOS: Gmail service
GOS --> EI: Gmail service

EI -> GLS: GmailLangchainService(gmail_service)
GLS -> GAPI: fetch_emails(max_results, query, after_date)
GAPI --> GLS: Raw email data (JSON)
GLS --> EI: List of email dictionaries

EI -> GLS: emails_to_documents(emails)
GLS --> EI: List of Langchain Documents
note right: Converts Gmail API format to Langchain Document objects\nwith metadata (sender, subject, date, email_id, etc.)

EI -> EVS: add_documents(documents, skip_duplicates=True)
EVS -> EVS: _load_indexed_ids() - Check duplicates
EVS -> ST: embed(texts) - Generate embeddings
ST --> EVS: Vector embeddings
EVS -> CDB: collection.add(documents, embeddings, metadatas, ids)
CDB --> EVS: Indexed successfully
EVS --> EI: Indexing results

EI --> EMC: Indexing complete
EMC --> FA: Success response
FA --> WB: Indexing complete

== Email Query Pipeline ==
U -> WB: Ask email question
WB -> FA: POST /chat (mode=email)
FA -> CC: process_chat_stream()

CC -> ERH: EmailRAGHandler.query()
ERH -> ERH: _extract_date_from_query() - Optional date filtering
ERH -> EVS: search(query, n_results, filter_metadata)
EVS -> CDB: similarity_search(query, n_results)
CDB --> EVS: Search results (documents + metadata + distances)
EVS --> ERH: Search results

ERH -> ERH: _build_context(search_results) - Format for LLM
ERH -> ERH: _build_sources(search_results) - Format for UI
ERH -> ERH: _filter_sources_by_date() - If date specified

ERH -> ERH: _generate_answer(query, context, sources)
ERH -> LLM: Generate answer with context
LLM --> ERH: AI-generated answer

ERH -> ERH: _filter_referenced_sources(answer, sources)
note right: Regex extracts email IDs from AI response\nOnly shows emails actually discussed

ERH --> CC: Final answer + filtered sources
CC -> CC: Stream answer to user
CC --> FA: Streaming response
FA --> WB: Real-time answer chunks

== Email Management Operations ==
U -> WB: View email stats
WB -> FA: GET /email/count
FA -> EMC: get_email_count()
EMC -> EI: get_unindexed_count()
EI -> GOS: get_gmail_service()
EI -> GLS: get_total_email_count()
EI -> EVS: get_stats()
EVS --> EI: Vector store stats
EI --> EMC: Email counts
EMC --> FA: Stats response

U -> WB: Search emails directly
WB -> FA: POST /email/search
FA -> EMC: search_emails()
EMC -> EVS: search(query, n_results)
EVS -> CDB: Vector search
CDB --> EVS: Results
EVS --> EMC: Search results
EMC --> FA: Formatted results

== Chunking & Processing Details ==

note over ST
**Chunking Strategy:**
- No explicit chunking in email pipeline
- Each email is treated as one document
- Full email content preserved
- Metadata includes: sender, subject, date, email_id, thread_id
- Embeddings generated on full email text
end note

note over GLS
**Document Conversion:**
- Gmail API → Langchain Document
- page_content: Full email body text
- metadata: sender, subject, date, labels, email_id, etc.
- No text splitting - emails kept whole
end note

note over ERH
**RAG Context Building:**
- Multiple emails combined into single context
- Each email formatted with headers:
  "═══════════════════════════════════════════════
   📧 EMAIL #X [REF: email_id]
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
   📌 Subject: {subject}
   👤 From: {sender}
   📅 Date: {date}
   📝 Email Content: {body[:1500]}"
end note

note over ERH
**Source Filtering:**
- Regex pattern: r'(?:REF|Reference):\s*\[?([a-f0-9]+)\]?'
- Matches: "Reference: [19c3eaf476a92a41]" or "Reference: 19c3eaf476a92a41"
- Only emails mentioned in AI response are shown
- Prevents showing irrelevant retrieved emails
end note

== Error Handling & Fallbacks ==
note over ERH
**Fallback Mechanisms:**
- If no emails found: Return "no relevant emails" message
- If LLM fails: Return fallback answer from retrieved blocks
- If reference filtering fails: Show all sources as fallback
- If OAuth expires: Prompt user to re-authenticate
end note

@enduml